Fix for FORTE 3.3.0: deleting a running IO configuration block (GPIOChip, PWMChip) crashed FORTE.
~IOConfigFBController calls deInit(nullptr, true), which went on to stopped() and set STATUS(): a
pure virtual of the derived block, already destroyed in the base destructor, so the call jumped to
address 0 (SIGSEGV; gdb on the filling Pi, 3 Nov). A deployment from the IDE deletes the running
resource first, so every redeployment of a program with IO crashed FORTE. When destructing, only the
controller is stopped and deleted now. Applied by build-runtime.ps1.

diff --git a/core/src/io/configFB/io_configFB_controller.cpp b/core/src/io/configFB/io_configFB_controller.cpp
index 3d25dd1..28dbecc 100644
--- a/core/src/io/configFB/io_configFB_controller.cpp
+++ b/core/src/io/configFB/io_configFB_controller.cpp
@@ -173,8 +173,16 @@ namespace forte::io {
     }
 
     if (paIsDestructing) {
+      // Called from the destructor: the derived block is gone already, and STATUS() (pure virtual
+      // here) would call nothing. Only the controller is stopped and deleted.
       mPerformRestart = false;
-      stopped(paECET);
+      mController->mDelegate = nullptr;
+      if (mController->isAlive()) {
+        mController->end();
+      }
+      delete mController;
+      mController = nullptr;
+      mStarting = false;
     } else {
       onStop(paECET);
     }
